/*
    Budget vs. Actuals across mismatched grain (requirement #5).
    Fact Budget: month x category x region.
    Fact Sales (Actuals): day x SKU x customer.

    Rule: Budget must not fabricate precision it doesn't have. When a report
    drills below budget's native grain (e.g. to a single SKU or a single
    customer), Budget blanks out rather than silently dividing evenly.

    Display Folder: "Budget vs Actual"
*/

Budget Amount (USD) :=
CALCULATE (
    SUM ( 'Fact Budget'[BudgetAmountUSD] ),
    -- Bridge Actuals' fine-grained filter context (e.g. a specific Product)
    -- up to Budget's coarser grain (ProductCategory) via TREATAS, so a
    -- Product-level slicer still finds the right Budget row.
    TREATAS (
        VALUES ( 'Dim Product'[ProductCategoryKey] ),
        'Fact Budget'[ProductCategoryKey]
    ),
    TREATAS (
        VALUES ( 'Dim Geography'[RegionKey] ),
        'Fact Budget'[RegionKey]
    )
)

Actuals Amount (USD) :=
[Net Revenue]   -- already in local currency; wrap with the currency calc group for USD
-- Description: Actuals, same grain as Fact Sales, for comparison against Budget Amount.

Budget vs Actual Variance :=
[Actuals Amount (USD)] - [Budget Amount (USD)]

Budget Amount (Grain-Safe) :=
-- Returns BLANK when the report is sliced below Budget's native grain
-- (SKU or Customer), instead of a misleading evenly-divided number.
VAR IsBelowCategoryGrain =
    ISINSCOPE ( 'Dim Product'[ProductKey] )          -- SKU-level, finer than Category
VAR IsBelowRegionGrain =
    ISINSCOPE ( 'Dim Customer'[CustomerBK] )          -- Customer-level, finer than Region
RETURN
    IF (
        IsBelowCategoryGrain || IsBelowRegionGrain,
        BLANK (),
        [Budget Amount (USD)]
    )

/*
    If the business later asks for an ALLOCATED budget at SKU level (e.g. to
    show "implied SKU budget" based on historical sales mix), that is a
    DIFFERENT, explicitly-named measure:

    Budget Amount (Allocated to SKU) :=
    VAR CategoryBudget = [Budget Amount (USD)]
    VAR CategoryActualsTotal =
        CALCULATE ( [Actuals Amount (USD)], ALLEXCEPT ( 'Dim Product', 'Dim Product'[ProductCategoryKey] ) )
    VAR SkuActuals = [Actuals Amount (USD)]
    RETURN
        CategoryBudget * DIVIDE ( SkuActuals, CategoryActualsTotal )

    This must never be named just "Budget Amount" - an allocated number and a
    blanked-out number answer different questions, and silently swapping one
    for the other is exactly the kind of per-report logic drift this model
    exists to prevent.
*/
